# Every path, one owner. The repository has a single maintainer, so this file
# exists to make review required rather than to route it: without an owner,
# GitHub's branch protection has nobody to ask.
*       @gufranco

# The two files that decide what everything else is checked against. A change to
# either one changes what "correct" means for the whole package.
/conformance/hardware.json      @gufranco
/conformance/divergences.json   @gufranco

# What identifies a cartridge before a byte of it is read. A wrong entry here
# means the wrong file is disassembled and a protocol nobody's hardware has is
# reported as though it were real.
/cartridges.manifest.json       @gufranco
